  "term": "FSD",
  "definition": "FSD stands for functional somatic disorder, a term for persistent and distressing physical symptoms lasting more than three months that are not explained by another medical or psychiatric condition. It is described as a problem of altered bodily functioning rather than simply a diagnosis made only after ruling everything else out, and it may involve one body system or several.",
